# Necrotic Ooze has the activated abilities of the creature cards in graveyards only. Opalescence makes "each other non-Aura
# enchantment" a creature - a permanent, never a card in a graveyard (CR 611.3a, 613.1d: a static ability of a permanent
# affects permanents unless it says otherwise) - so Assault Formation, which Bot2 discards to its hand size on turn 2, is
# an enchantment card in a graveyard and gives the Ooze nothing: with {2}{G} open on turn 5 the Ooze offers neither of its
# abilities (the refusals). Walking Ballista, a creature card in Bot1's graveyard since turn 1, does give its abilities:
# "{4}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature" is activated (the positive control), and the Ooze, a creature Opalescence
# does not touch, is a 5/4.

